{"id": "EUVD-2020-31281", "enisaUuid": "7557fda7-bbcf-36c0-b596-cd38515104ac", "description": "office-converter through 1.0.2 contains an OS command injection vulnerability that allows attackers to execute commands by supplying a crafted fileName to generatePdf() or generateHtml(). Attackers can embed $(...), backticks, or a closing quote with shell metacharacters in the file name, which is concatenated into an unoconv command run via child_process.exec(), executing commands with Node.js process privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T14:16:28", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-9p64-h5q4-phpm", "https://github.com/vworld4u/office-converter/pull/9", "https://github.com/vworld4u/office-converter/blob/b1ea855d0001dc7a5d66343698634dbc06b72c2d/index.js#L19-L20", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/office-converter-through-1.0.2-os-command-injection-via-filename-in-generatepdf"], "aliases": ["CVE-2020-37282", "GHSA-869r-fxq2-q8qx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 3.04, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a6c02008-3a36-3422-a553-ba99316d1216", "product": {"name": "office-converter", "vendor": {"name": "vworld4u"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.0.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cf07ec22-a131-36bd-b8a9-b56efc21a8f6", "vendor": {"name": "vworld4u"}}], "isExploited": false}